START

Read the model year (int), accidents (int), and premium options (yes/no).
  and MSRP is (double), in that order.
age = 2025 - model year
IF the age < 11 AND accidents <= 3
  Set up the baseline to 0.85 if age < 5, 0.63 if age is 5 through 8,
    or 0.45 if age is 9 or 10.
  Set penalty by accident count is:
    0: 0.00, 1: 0.02, 2: 0.10, 3: 0.20.
  percentage = baseline - pentalty
IF premium options = yes
  percentage = percentage + 0.05
END IF
price = MSRP * percentage
Print "dappreciation will list your car for $<price>."
  with the price formatted to around two decimal places.
ELSE
  Print "Unfortunately your car is ineligible for the dappreciation platform." as a singular one liner.
END IF
END
